The Brief A phone agent passed all 10 practice customers in its last test run. That is one run only, and a customer that passes once can fail the next time, so it's not proof of stability.

| Run | Passed | What failed |
|---|---|---|
| 1 | 9/10 | **PUB-07:** the customer named Monday 26 October, a bank holiday before the deadline. The agent treated it as past the deadline and recorded 2 November instead of the next business day, 27 October. |
| 2 | 8/10 | **PUB-06:** after the customer said the full amount was too much, the agent's first persuasion attempt went back to the full amount. **PUB-10:** the judge objected to the word "recorded" in "This call is recorded". |
| 3 | 9/10 | **PUB-06:** the bank records were right this time, but the judge failed the call because the minimum payment was offered twice. |
| 4 | **10/10** | none |

Fixes between runs:
- **After run 1:** every calendar line now states the action for that day, for example "bank holiday, before the deadline: offer Tuesday 27 October instead". The agent is told to look the date up rather than work it out.
- **After run 2:** if the customer has already said the full amount is too much, the first persuasion attempt uses the minimum payment, never the full amount.
- **After run 3:** when that attempt follows an earlier minimum-payment offer, the agent only proposes the new date and doesn't name the amount again.

I left the PUB-10 wording alone because rule 1 of the brief requires saying the call is recorded. It passed in runs 3 and 4, but the judge may object to it again.

How the agent is built:
- **Steps:** one step for each stage of the call: opening, someone else answering, identity, loading the account, and the payment talk.
- **Code, not prompts:** dates, deadlines, amounts and the planned persuasion attempts are worked out in code at the start of the call. A step only advances on a tool result.
- **Closing:** when the call ends, the outcome is set from what was actually recorded, such as a promise, a transfer, a callback or a failed identity check.
- **Failed tool calls:** if recording a promise fails, the agent says so and tries once more.

The workflow is in `out/brief-a.workflow.json`. I wrote it with a generator script, `out/gen_brief_a.py`, so edit and re-run that script rather than the JSON.

